hadiths[94]{hadithnumber,text}:
"22085","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Uqba narrated to us, Kurayb informed me that he asked Usama ibn Zayd, he said: I said: Inform me how you did on the evening you rode behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: We came to the ravine where the people halt for Maghrib, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made his camel kneel, then he urinated, he said, he poured water, then he called for ablution water and performed ablution not very thorough, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah prayer, he said: Prayer is ahead of you, he said: Then he rode until he came to Muzdalifa and established Maghrib, then the people halted in their dwellings and did not unpack until he established Isha and prayed, then the people unpacked, he said: So I said: How did you do when you entered the morning, he said: al-Fadl ibn Abbas rode behind him, and I set out among the forerunners of Quraysh on my feet."
"22086","Yahya ibn Ishaq and Affan said: Wuhayb narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Tawus narrated to us, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, from Usama ibn Zayd, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No riba in what was hand to hand, he said, meaning riba is only in deferment."
"22087","Affan narrated to us, Aban narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Hakam narrated to me, from the freed slave of Qudama ibn Mazun, from the freed slave of Usama ibn Zayd, that he set out with Usama to Wadi al-Qura seeking wealth of his, and he would fast Monday and Thursday, so his freed slave said to him: Why do you fast Monday and Thursday while you are an old man grown thin, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to fast Monday and Thursday, so he was asked about that, and he said: The deeds of the people are presented on Monday and Thursday."
"22088","Hushaym ibn Bashir narrated to us, Husayn narrated to us, from Abi Zibyan, he said: I heard Usama ibn Zayd narrating, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent us to al-Huraqa of Juhayna, he said: So we attacked them at dawn and fought them, and there was among them a man, when the people advanced he was among the fiercest of them against us, and when they retreated he was their protector, he said: So I and a man from the Ansar overwhelmed him, he said: When we overwhelmed him he said: There is no god but Allah, so the Ansari held back from him, and I killed him, so that reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: O Usama did you kill him after he said: There is no god but Allah, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah he was only seeking refuge from killing, so he repeated it to me until I wished I had not embraced Islam except that day."
"22089","Hushaym narrated to us, Sulayman al-Taymi informed us, from Abi Uthman al-Nahdi, from Usama ibn Zayd, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have not left after me a trial more harmful to my ummah, against men, than women."
"22090","Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ali ibn Husayn, from Amr ibn Uthman, from Usama ibn Zayd, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The Muslim does not inherit the disbeliever, nor does the disbeliever inherit the Muslim."
"22091","Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwa, from Usama ibn Zayd, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked over upon a fortress of the fortresses of Madinah and said: Do you see what I see, I see the places of tribulations among your houses like the places of raindrops."
"22092","Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Uqba, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Usama ibn Zayd informed me that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mounted him behind him from Arafah, then when he came to the ravine he descended and urinated, and he did not say: he poured water, so I poured upon him and he performed a light ablution, so I said: Prayer, so he said: Prayer is ahead of you, he said: Then he came to Muzdalifa and prayed Maghrib, then they unpacked their saddles, and I helped him, then he prayed Isha."
"22093","Sufyan ibn Uyayna narrated to us, Amr, meaning Ibn Dinar, narrated to us, from Abi Salih, he said: I heard Abu Said saying: Gold for gold weight for weight, he said: So I met Ibn Abbas and said: What you say, is it something you found in the Book of Allah or heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: It is not something I found in the Book of Allah or heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), but Usama ibn Zayd informed me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Riba is in deferment."
"22094","Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr, from Amir ibn Sad, he said: A man came asking Sad about the plague, so Usama ibn Zayd said: I will narrate to you about it, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: This is a punishment, or like that, Allah sent it upon people before you, or a group of the Children of Israel, so it comes sometimes and goes sometimes, so if it occurs in a land do not enter upon it, and if it occurs in a land do not exit fleeing from it."
"22095","Rawh narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Hafsa narrated to us, al-Zuhri narrated to us, from Ali ibn Husayn, from Amr ibn Uthman, from Usama ibn Zayd, that he said: O Messenger of Allah where will you stay tomorrow Allah willing, and that was at the time of the conquest, so he said: Has Aqil left for us any dwelling, then he said: The disbeliever does not inherit the believer, nor does the believer inherit the disbeliever."
"22096","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Thabit ibn Qays Abu Ghusn narrated to us, Abu Said al-Maqburi narrated to me, Usama ibn Zayd narrated to me, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would fast days continuously until it was said he does not break, and break days until he would hardly fast except two days of the week, if they were in his fasting, otherwise he fasted them, and he would not fast of the months what he fasts of Shaban, so I said: O Messenger of Allah you fast almost not breaking, and break almost not fasting except two days, if they enter in your fasting, otherwise you fast them, he said: Which two days, he said, I said: Monday and Thursday, he said: Those are two days in which deeds are presented to the Lord of the worlds, and I love my deed to be presented while I am fasting, he said, I said: And I never saw you fasting of the months what you fast of Shaban, he said: That is a month people neglect between Rajab and Ramadan, and it is a month in which deeds are raised to the Lord of the worlds, so I love my deed to be raised while I am fasting."
"22097","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: I said to Ata: Did you hear Ibn Abbas, then he mentioned a story, but I heard him saying: Usama ibn Zayd informed me that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he entered the House supplicated in all its corners, and did not pray in it until he exited, then when he exited he bowed two units facing the Kaba and said: This is the qibla."
"22098","Yaqub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, Said ibn Ubayd ibn al-Sabbaq narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Usama ibn Zayd, from his father Usama ibn Zayd, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) became gravely ill I descended, and the people descended with me to Madinah, so I entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he had fallen silent not speaking, so he began raising his hands to the sky then pouring them upon me, I knew he was supplicating for me."
"22099","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, Qays ibn Sad informed us, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, from Usama, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) poured forth from Arafah with Usama behind him, so he kept reining his mount until its temples almost touch, and perhaps Hammad said: strike the front of the saddle, while he was saying: O people upon you is tranquility and dignity, for righteousness is not in hurrying the camels."
"22100","Affan narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, Ibn Tawus narrated to us, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, from Usama ibn Zayd, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No riba in what was hand to hand."
"22101","Qutaybah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Abi Za'idah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Usamah ibn Zayd, who said: I entered with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, upon Abdullah ibn Ubayy during his illness to visit him, and the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to him: I used to forbid you from loving the Jews. Abdullah said: As'ad ibn Zurarah hated them, then died."
"22102","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, al-Mas'udi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ali Abu Ja'far narrated to us, from Usamah ibn Zayd, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed in the House."
"22103","Ya'qub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to me, from his father, from Usamah ibn Zayd, who said: I was riding behind the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on the evening of Arafah. He said: When the sun set, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, moved on, and when he heard the crushing noise of the people behind him, he said: Gently, O people, calmness is upon you, for righteousness is not in hurrying. He said: Whenever the people crowded upon the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he hastened, and when he found an opening he galloped, until he passed by the mountain pass about which many people claim that he prayed in it. He dismounted there and urinated, not pouring water as they say, then I brought him the small water-skin and he performed ablution. Then he said: I said, the prayer, O Messenger of Allah. He said: The prayer is ahead of you. He said: So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, rode on and did not pray until he came to Muzdalifah, where he dismounted and combined the two prayers, Maghrib and the last Isha."
"22104","Ya'qub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, Ibrahim ibn Uqbah narrated to me, from Kurayb, freedman of Abdullah ibn Abbas, from Usamah ibn Zayd, who said: I was riding behind the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on the evening of Arafah. When the sun set, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, moved on, and when he heard the crushing noise of the people behind him, he said: Gently, O people, calmness is upon you, for righteousness is not in hurrying. He said: Whenever the people crowded upon the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he hastened, and when he found an opening he galloped, until he passed by the mountain pass about which many people claim that he prayed in it. He dismounted there and urinated, not pouring water as they say, then I brought him the small water-skin and he performed ablution. Then he said: I said, the prayer, O Messenger of Allah. He said: The prayer is ahead of you. He said: So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, rode on and did not pray until he came to Muzdalifah, where he dismounted and combined the two prayers, Maghrib and the last Isha."
"22105","Ya'qub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, Ubaydullah ibn Ali ibn Abi Rafi' narrated to me, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab, Usamah ibn Zayd narrated to me that he heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: There is no riba except in deferment."
"22106","Abu Salamah al-Khuza'i narrated to us, Malik informed us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir and Abu al-Nadr, freedman of Umar ibn Ubaydullah ibn Ma'mar, from Amir ibn Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas, from his father, that he asked Usamah ibn Zayd what he had heard from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, concerning the plague. Usamah said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: It is a punishment sent upon a group of the Children of Israel, or upon a group of those who were before you, the doubt is in the hadith. If you hear of it in a land, do not go forward to it, and if it occurs in a land while you are in it, do not leave fleeing from it. Abu al-Nadr said in his hadith: Nothing brings you out except fleeing from it."
"22107","Hasan ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Abu Ma'shar narrated to us, from Sulaym, freedman of Banu Layth, and he was old, who said: Marwan ibn al-Hakam passed by Usamah ibn Zayd while he was praying, and Marwan mimicked him. Abu Ma'shar said: He had met both of them. Usamah said: O Marwan, I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Allah does not love every foul-mouthed vulgar person."
"22108","Harun ibn Ma'ruf narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, that Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir narrated to him, that he was informed by one who heard Usamah ibn Zayd say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, combined Maghrib and Isha at Muzdalifah."
"22109","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Ali ibn Husayn, from Amr ibn Uthman, from Usamah ibn Zayd, who said: I said, O Messenger of Allah, where shall we stay tomorrow during his Hajj. He said: Has Aqil left us any dwelling. Then he said: We shall stay tomorrow, Allah willing, at the Khayf of Banu Kinanah, meaning al-Muhassab, where Quraysh had sworn upon disbelief. That is because Banu Kinanah allied with Quraysh against Banu Hashim that they would not marry them, nor trade with them, nor shelter them. Then he said at that time: The disbeliever does not inherit from the Muslim, nor the Muslim from the disbeliever. Al-Zuhri said: Al-Khayf is the valley."
"22110","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, that Usamah ibn Zayd informed him that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, rode a donkey with a saddle upon which was a Fadak-made velvet cloth, and he took Usamah ibn Zayd behind him, while visiting Sa'd ibn Ubadah among Banu al-Harith ibn al-Khazraj, before the battle of Badr, until he passed by a gathering containing a mix of Muslims, polytheists, idol-worshippers and Jews, among them Abdullah ibn Ubayy, and in the gathering was Abdullah ibn Rawahah. When the dust of the mount covered the gathering, Abdullah ibn Ubayy covered his nose with his cloak, then said: Do not raise dust over us. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, greeted them, then stopped and dismounted, and invited them to Allah and recited the Quran to them. Abdullah ibn Ubayy said to him: O man, there is nothing better than this; if what you say is true, do not harm us in our gatherings, and return to your dwelling; whoever of us comes to you, relate to him. Abdullah ibn Rawahah said: Come upon us in our gatherings, for we love that. Then the Muslims, polytheists and Jews reviled one another until they were about to attack one another. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, kept calming them, then rode his mount until he entered upon Sa'd ibn Ubadah and said: O Sa'd, did you not hear what Abu Hubab said, meaning Abdullah ibn Ubayy, such and such. He said: Pardon him, O Messenger of Allah, and overlook. By Allah, Allah has given you what He has given you, and the people of this pond had agreed to crown him and wrap him with the headband, but when Allah rejected that by the truth He gave you, he choked with that, and that is what made him do what you saw. So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, pardoned him."
"22111","Hajjaj narrated to us, Layth, meaning Ibn Sa'd, narrated to us, Uqayl narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, from Urwah, that Usamah ibn Zayd informed him, and he mentioned its meaning, except that he said: The people of this pond had gathered."
"22112","Abu al-Yaman narrated to us, Shu'ayb informed us, from al-Zuhri, Urwah ibn al-Zubayr informed me, that Usamah ibn Zayd informed him that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, rode a donkey with a saddle upon which was a Fadak-made velvet cloth, and took Usamah ibn Zayd behind him, visiting Sa'd ibn Ubadah among Banu al-Khazraj before the battle of Badr, and he mentioned it, and he said: al-Bahrah."
"22113","Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri narrated to us, Haywah narrated to us, Ayyash ibn Abbas informed me, that Abu al-Nadr narrated to him, from Amir ibn Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas, that Usamah ibn Zayd informed his father Sa'd ibn Malik. He said: He said to him: A man came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: I practice withdrawal from my wife. He said: Why. He said: Out of pity for her child, or for her children. He said: If it is so, then no; that did not harm Persia nor Rome."
"22114","Haytham narrated to us, Abdullah said: I heard it myself from al-Haytham ibn Kharijah, Rushdin ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Uqayl, from Ibn Shihab, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Usamah ibn Zayd, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that Jibril, peace be upon him, when he descended upon the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, taught him ablution. When he finished his ablution, he took a handful of water and sprinkled it toward the private area. He said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to sprinkle after his ablution."
"22115","Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from al-Harith, from Kurayb, freedman of Ibn Abbas, from Usamah ibn Zayd, who said: I entered upon the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while he was gloomy, and I asked him what was wrong with him. He said: Jibril has not come to me for three days. Then a puppy was found among his houses, and he ordered it killed. Then Jibril, peace be upon him, appeared to him, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, rejoiced toward him when he saw him. He said: You did not come to me. He said: We do not enter a house in which there is a dog, nor images."
"22116","Husayn narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from al-Harith ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Kurayb, freedman of Ibn Abbas, from Usamah ibn Zayd, who said: I entered upon the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while he was gloomy, and he mentioned the meaning of the hadith of Uthman ibn Umar, except that he said: He has not come to me for three days."
"22117","Abu Sa'id, freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated to us, Qays ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us, Jami' ibn Shaddad narrated to us, from Kulthum al-Khuza'i, from Usamah ibn Zayd, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to me: Admit my companions to me. They entered upon him, and he uncovered the veil, then said: May Allah curse the Jews and Christians; they took the graves of their prophets as mosques."
"22118","Surayj narrated to us, Qays narrated to us, from Jami', except that he said: They entered upon him while he was wrapped in a Ma'afiri cloak, and he did not say: and the Christians."
"22119","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Asim al-Ahwal, who said: I heard Abu Uthman narrating from Usamah ibn Zayd, who said: One of his daughters sent to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that a boy of hers, a son or a daughter, was dying, so witness us. He said: He sent to her conveying greetings and saying: To Allah belongs what He took and what He gave, and everything with Him is for an appointed term, so let her be patient and seek reward. She then sent swearing upon him, so he stood and we stood. The boy was lifted to the lap, or in the lap, of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while his soul was rattling. Among the people were Sa'd ibn Ubadah and Ubayy, I think. The eyes of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, overflowed. Sa'd said to him: What is this, O Messenger of Allah. He said: This is mercy which Allah places in the hearts of whom He wills of His servants, and Allah only shows mercy to the merciful among His servants."
"22120","Ahmad ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Yazid ibn Abdullah ibn Qusayt, from Muhammad ibn Usamah, from his father, who said: Ja'far, Ali and Zayd ibn Harithah gathered. Ja'far said: I am the most beloved of you to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. Ali said: I am the most beloved of you to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. Zayd said: I am the most beloved of you to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. They said: Let us go to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, to ask him. Usamah ibn Zayd said: They came seeking permission. He said: Go out and see who these are. I said: This is Ja'far, Ali and Zayd; what shall I say, father. He said: Admit them. They entered and said: Who is most beloved to you. He said: Fatimah. They said: We ask you about men. He said: As for you, O Ja'far, your form resembles my form and your character resembles my character, and you are of me and my tree. As for you, O Ali, you are my in-law and father of my child, and I am of you and you are of me. As for you, O Zayd, you are my freedman, of me and to me, and the most beloved of the people to me."
"22121","Sufyan narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Abi Yazid, who heard Ibn Abbas say: Usamah ibn Zayd narrated to me, from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and once he said: Usamah informed me that he said: Riba is in deferment."
"22122","Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, Asim narrated to us, from Abu Uthman al-Nahdi, from Usamah ibn Zayd, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was brought Umaymah, daughter of Zaynab, while her soul was rattling as if in a water-skin. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: To Allah belongs what He took, and to Allah belongs what He gave, and all is for an appointed term. His eyes shed tears. Sa'd ibn Ubadah said to him: O Messenger of Allah, do you weep; did you not forbid weeping. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: It is only mercy which Allah placed in the hearts of His servants, and Allah only shows mercy to the merciful among His servants."
"22123","Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Umarah, from Abu al-Sha'tha, who said: I went out for Hajj and entered the House. When I was at the two pillars I moved until I stuck to the wall. He said: Ibn Umar came until he stood beside me and prayed four. He said: When he prayed I said to him: Where did the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, pray in the House. He said: Here; Usamah ibn Zayd informed me that he prayed. He said: I said, how many did he pray. He said: On this I find myself blaming myself that I stayed with him a lifetime and did not ask him how many he prayed. When the next year came, he said: I went out for Hajj. He said: I came until I stood in his station. He said: Ibn al-Zubayr came until he stood beside me and kept jostling me until he pushed me out of it, then prayed four in it."
"22124","Isma'il narrated to us, Hisham, meaning al-Dastuwa'i, narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, from Umar ibn al-Hakam ibn Thawban, that the freedman of Qudamah ibn Maz'un narrated to him, that the freedman of Usamah ibn Zayd narrated to him, that Usamah ibn Zayd used to go out to property of his in Wadi al-Qura, fasting Mondays and Thursdays. I said to him: Why do you fast while traveling when you have grown old and thin. He said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to fast Mondays and Thursdays. I said: O Messenger of Allah, why do you fast Mondays and Thursdays. He said: Deeds are presented on Monday and on Thursday."
"22125","Isma'il ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Sulayman al-Taymi, from Abu Uthman al-Nahdi, from Usamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I stood at the gate of Paradise, and most of those who entered it were the poor, while the people of wealth, and Yahya ibn Sa'id and others said: except the people of wealth, are detained, except the people of Fire, for they have been ordered to the Fire. And I stood at the gate of Fire, and most of those who enter it are women."
"22126","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, my father narrated to me, who said: Usamah was asked about the pace of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in the Farewell Hajj, while I was present. He said: His pace was al-anaq; when he found an opening he galloped, and al-nass is above al-anaq, and I was riding behind him."
"22127","Ya'la ibn Ubayd narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Abu Wa'il, who said: It was said to Usamah: Will you not speak to Uthman. He said: You think I do not speak to him except in your hearing; I do not speak to him concerning what is between me and him without opening a matter I would not like to be the first to open. By Allah, I shall not say to a man that he is the best of people, even if he is a ruler over me, after I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say. They said: What did you hear him say. He said: I heard him say: A man will be brought on the Day of Resurrection and cast into the Fire, and his intestines will spill out, and he will go round with them in the Fire as the donkey goes round its millstone. The people of Fire will gather round him and say: O so-and-so, what is wrong with you, what befell you; did you not command us to good and forbid us from evil. He said: I used to command you to good and not do it, and forbid you from evil and do it."
"22128","Waki' narrated to us, Salih ibn Abi al-Akhdar narrated to me, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Usamah ibn Zayd, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent me to a village called Ubna, and said: Come to it in the morning, then burn."
"22129","Abu Amir narrated to us, Zuhayr, meaning Ibn Muhammad, narrated to us, from Abdullah, meaning Ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from the son of Usamah ibn Zayd, that his father Usamah said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, clothed me with a thick Coptic garment that was among what Dihyah al-Kalbi had gifted, and I clothed my wife with it. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to me: Why have you not worn the Coptic garment. I said: O Messenger of Allah, I clothed my wife with it. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to me: Command her to put an undergarment beneath it, for I fear it describes the size of her bones."
"22130","Arim ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, Mu'tamir narrated to us, from his father, who said: I heard Abu Tamimah narrating from Abu Uthman al-Nahdi, Abu Uthman narrating to him from Usamah ibn Zayd, who said: The Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to take me and seat me on his thigh, and seat al-Hasan ibn Ali on his other thigh, then embrace us, then say: O Allah, have mercy on them, for I have mercy on them. My father said: Ali ibn al-Madini said: He is al-Salli, of Anazah to Rabi'ah, meaning Abu Tamimah al-Salli."
"22131","Zakariyya ibn Adi narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Muhammad ibn Usamah ibn Zayd, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, clothed me with a thick Coptic garment from what Dihyah al-Kalbi had gifted him. I clothed my wife with it. He said: Why have you not worn the Coptic garment. I said: I clothed my wife with it. He said: Command her to put an undergarment beneath it, for I fear it describes the size of her bones."
"22132","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Sufyan informed us, from Asim, from Abu Uthman al-Nahdi, from Usamah ibn Zayd, who said: The daughter of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent that her son was being taken, so come to us. He sent conveying greetings and saying: To Allah belongs what He took, and to Allah belongs what He gave, and everything with Him is for a named term. He said: She sent to him swearing upon him that he must come. He said: He stood, and we stood with him: Mu'adh ibn Jabal, Ubayy ibn Ka'b and Sa'd ibn Ubadah. He said: He took the boy while his soul was rattling. He said: His eyes shed tears. Sa'd said: O Messenger of Allah, what is this. He said: This is mercy which Allah placed in the hearts of His servants, and Allah only shows mercy to the merciful among His servants."
"22133","Ahmad ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us, Ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Dhi'b, from Shu'bah, from Ibn Abbas, from Usamah ibn Zayd, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, took him behind him on the day of Arafah until he entered the mountain pass, then poured water and performed ablution, then rode and did not pray."
"22134","Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Thabit ibn Qays informed me, from Abu Sa'id al-Maqburi, from Usamah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to fast Mondays and Thursdays."
"22135","Yazid narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Dhi'b, from al-Zibriqan, that a group of Quraysh were passed by Zayd ibn Thabit while they were gathered, and they sent to him two of their boys asking him about the middle prayer. He said: It is Asr. Two men of them stood to him and asked him. He said: It is Zuhr. Then they went to Usamah ibn Zayd and asked him. He said: It is Zuhr; the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to pray Zuhr at midday, and none would be behind him except a row or two rows of people, during their midday rest and their trade. So Allah the Exalted revealed: Maintain the prayers and the middle prayer, and stand for Allah devoutly. He said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Men shall desist, or I shall burn their houses."
"22136","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Azrah, from al-Sha'bi, from Usamah, that he narrated to him, who said: I was riding behind the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he poured forth from Arafat, and his mount did not lift its foot hastening until it reached Jam'."
"22137","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Asim, from Abu Wa'il, who said: It was said to Usamah ibn Zayd, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: A man who was obeyed in acts of disobedience to Allah the Exalted will be brought and cast into the Fire, and his intestines will spill out, and he will turn round in it as the donkey turns round in the millstone. The people of his obedience among men will come upon him and say: O so-and-so, where is what you commanded us with. He will say: I used to command you with a matter and oppose you to another."
"22138","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Dawud ibn Abi al-Furat narrated to us, from Ibrahim, meaning al-Sa'igh, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, Usamah ibn Zayd narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Riba is in deferment."
"22139","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, Yahya ibn Qays al-Mazini informed me, who said: I asked Ata about a dinar for a dinar with excess between them, and a dirham for a dirham. He said: Ibn Abbas used to permit it. Ibn al-Zubayr said: Ibn Abbas narrates what he did not hear from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. It reached Ibn Abbas, and he said: I did not hear it from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, but Usamah ibn Zayd narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There is no riba except in deferment, or in exchange."
"22140","Abu Qatan narrated to us, al-Mas'udi narrated to us, from Abu Ja'far, from Usamah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed in the Ka'bah."
"22141","Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: Habib ibn Abi Thabit informed us, he said: I heard Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrating that he heard Usamah ibn Zayd narrating to Sa'd that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: If you hear of the plague in a land, do not enter it, and if it occurs in a land while you are in it, do not leave it. He said: I said: Did you hear him narrating to Sa'd while he does not deny. He said: Yes."
"22142","Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, Asim narrated to us, Abu Uthman al-Nahdi narrated to me, from Usamah ibn Zayd, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was brought Umaymah, daughter of Zaynab, while her soul was rattling as if in a water-skin. He said: To Allah belongs what He took, and to Allah belongs what He gave, and all is for an appointed term. He said: His eyes shed tears. Sa'd ibn Ubadah said to him: O Messenger of Allah, do you weep; did you not forbid weeping. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: It is only mercy which Allah placed in the hearts of His servants, and Allah only shows mercy to the merciful among His servants."
"22143","Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Shaqiq, from Usamah ibn Zayd, who said: They said to him: Will you not enter upon this man and speak to him. He said: Do you not see that I do not speak to him except making you hear. By Allah, I have spoken to him concerning what is between me and him without opening a matter I would not like to be the first to open. I shall not say to a man under me as a ruler that he is the best of people, after I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: A man will be brought on the Day of Resurrection and cast into the Fire, and the intestines of his belly will spill out, and he will go round with them in the Fire as the donkey goes round the millstone. He said: The people of Fire will gather to him and say: O so-and-so, did you not command us to good and forbid us from evil. He said: He will say: Yes, I used to command good and not do it, and forbid evil and do it."
"22144","Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Umarah, from Abu al-Sha'tha, who said: I went out for Hajj and came until I entered the House. When I was between the two pillars I moved until I stuck to the wall. Ibn Umar came and prayed beside me, praying four. When he prayed I said to him: Where did the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, pray in the House. He said: Usamah ibn Zayd informed me that he prayed here. I said: How many did he pray. He said: On this I find myself blaming myself that I stayed with him a lifetime and did not ask him how many he prayed. Then I performed Hajj the next year and came until I stood in his station. Ibn al-Zubayr came until he stood beside me and kept jostling me until he pushed me out of it, then prayed four in it."
"22145","Ya'la narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Abu Zabyan, Usamah ibn Zayd narrated to us, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent us as an expedition to al-Huraqat. They sensed us and fled. We caught a man, and when we overcame him he said: There is no god but Allah. We struck him until we killed him. Something of that occurred in myself, so I mentioned it to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: Who will be for you with There is no god but Allah on the Day of Resurrection. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, he only said it from fear of weapons and killing. He said: Did you not split open his heart to know whether for that or not. Who will be for you with There is no god but Allah on the Day of Resurrection. He said: He kept saying that until I wished I had not become Muslim except that day."
"22146","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Qays ibn Sa'd, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, from Usamah ibn Zayd, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, poured forth from Arafah while I was riding behind him. He kept reining his mount until its side almost struck the front of the saddle, saying: O people, calmness and dignity are upon you, for righteousness is not in hurrying camels."
"22147","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, Ibn Shihab narrated to us, from a cousin of Usamah ibn Zayd called Iyad, and the daughter of Usamah was under him. He said: A man who had come from some countryside was mentioned to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him; when he was near Madinah on part of the road, plague afflicted him. He said: That alarmed the people. He said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I hope its mountain pass will not rise upon us, meaning Madinah."
"22148","My father said: al-Hashimi and Ya'qub narrated it to us, and both alike said that he heard Usamah."
"22149","Abu Ma'mar narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, Ibn Shihab narrated to us, from a cousin of Usamah ibn Zayd called Iyad, and the daughter of Usamah was with him, and he mentioned the hadith likewise. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Some of them said Iyad ibn Sabra."
"22150","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Amir ibn Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas, from Usamah ibn Zayd, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: This plague is a punishment with which Allah destroyed the nations before you, and some of it remains in the earth, coming sometimes and going sometimes. If it occurs in a land, do not leave it, and if you hear of it in a land, do not come to it."
"22151","Abu al-Yaman narrated to us, Shu'ayb narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, Amir ibn Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas informed me that he heard Usamah ibn Zayd narrating to Sa'd that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, mentioned this pain, and he mentioned the hadith."
"22152","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, Ibn Shihab informed me, my father said: Abd al-A'la, from Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, from Ali ibn Husayn, from Amr ibn Uthman, from Usamah ibn Zayd, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The Muslim does not inherit from the disbeliever, nor the disbeliever inherit from the Muslim."
"22153","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, and Rawh, both said: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, he said: I said to Ata: I heard Ibn Abbas say: You were only commanded with circumambulation and were not commanded with entering. He said: He did not forbid entering it, but I heard him say: Usamah ibn Zayd informed me that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he entered the House supplicated in all its corners and did not pray in it until he left. When he left he bowed two rak'ahs facing the Ka'bah. Abd al-Razzaq said: This is the qiblah."
"22154","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Usamah, who said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, looked over a fortress of the fortresses of Madinah and said: Do you see what I see. They said: No. He said: I see trials falling among Madinah as rainfall falls."
"22155","Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, and Yazid said: Muhammad ibn Amr informed us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Amir ibn Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas, from Usamah ibn Zayd, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: If you hear of the plague in a land, do not enter upon it, and if it occurs while you are in a land, do not leave fleeing from it."
"22156","Waki' narrated to us, Umar ibn Dharr narrated to us, from Mujahid, from Usamah ibn Zayd, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, took him behind him from Arafah. He said: The people said: Our companion will inform us what he did. He said: Usamah said: When he moved from Arafah he held back the head of his mount until its head struck the middle of the saddle, or almost struck it, gesturing to the people with his hand: Calmness, calmness, calmness, until he came to Jam'. Then he took al-Fadl ibn Abbas behind him. He said: The people said: Our companion will inform us what the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, did. Al-Fadl said: He kept going a gentle pace as his pace yesterday, until he came upon the valley of Muhassir, then hastened in it until the earth became level with him."
"22157","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Malik narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ali ibn Husayn, from Umar ibn Uthman, from Usamah ibn Zayd, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said: The Muslim does not inherit from the disbeliever."
"22158","He said: I read upon Abd al-Rahman: Malik, from Musa ibn Uqbah, and Rawh narrated to us, from Malik, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Kurayb, freedman of Ibn Abbas, from Usamah ibn Zayd, that he heard him say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, moved from Arafah until, when he was at the mountain pass, he dismounted and urinated, then performed ablution without perfecting it. I said to him: The prayer. He said: The prayer is ahead of you. He rode, and when he came to Muzdalifah he dismounted and performed ablution, perfecting it. Then the prayer was established and he prayed Maghrib. Then every man made his camel kneel at his station. Then the prayer was established and he prayed it, and did not pray anything between them."
"22159","Isma'il narrated to us, Khalid al-Hadhdha informed us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from Usamah ibn Zayd, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Riba is only in deferment."
"22160","Isma'il narrated to us, Hisham al-Dastuwa'i informed us, Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, from Umar ibn al-Hakam ibn Thawban, that the freedman of Qudamah narrated to him, that a freedman of Usamah narrated to him, that Usamah ibn Zayd used to go out to his property in Wadi al-Qura, fasting Mondays and Thursdays. I said to him: Why do you fast while traveling when you have grown old and thin. He said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to fast Mondays and Thursdays. I said: O Messenger of Allah, you fast Mondays and Thursdays. He said: Deeds are presented on Monday and Thursday."
"22161","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Dhakwan, who said: Abu Sa'id al-Khudri sent me to Ibn Abbas. He said: Say to him concerning exchange: Did you hear from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, what we did not hear, or read in the Book of Allah what we did not read. He said: I do not say either, but I heard Usamah ibn Zayd narrating that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There is no riba except in debt, or he said: in deferment."
"22162","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, who said: I was in Madinah, and it reached me that the plague was in Kufah. He said: Ata ibn Yasar and more than one of the people of Madinah mentioned this hadith to me. He said: I said: Who narrates it. He said: They said: Amir ibn Sa'd, and he was absent. He said: I met Ibrahim ibn Sa'd. He said: I asked him about that. He said: I heard Usamah narrating to Sa'd that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: This pain is filth and punishment, or remnant of punishment, Habib doubted concerning it, with which people before you were punished. If it is in a land while you are in it, do not leave it, and if you hear of it in a land, do not enter it. He said: I said to him: Did you hear Usamah narrating to Sa'd without denial. He said: Yes."
"22163","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Sulayman, who said: I heard Abu Wa'il, who said: It was said to Usamah: Will you not speak to this. He said: I have spoken to him. I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: A man will be brought and thrown into the Fire, and he will grind in it as the donkey grinds with its millstone. The people of Fire will gather round him and say: O so-and-so, were you not commanding good and forbidding evil. He will say: I used to command good and not do it, and forbid evil and do it. Shu'bah said: Mansur narrated to me, from Abu Wa'il, from Usamah, similar to it, except that he added in it: The intestines of his belly will spill out."
"22164","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, Ibn Shihab informed us, from Ali ibn Husayn, from Amr ibn Uthman, from Usamah ibn Zayd, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The disbeliever does not inherit from the Muslim, nor the Muslim inherit from the disbeliever."
"22165","Hushaym narrated to us, Abd al-Malik informed us, Ata narrated to us, who said: Usamah ibn Zayd said: I was riding behind the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, at Arafat. He raised his hands supplicating, and his she-camel tilted, and its bridle fell. He said: He took the bridle with one of his hands while raising his other hand."
"22166","Hushaym narrated to us, Abd al-Malik narrated to us, from Ata, who said: Usamah ibn Zayd said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he left the House, turn his face toward the door and say: This is the qiblah, this is the qiblah."
"22167","Hushaym narrated to us, Abd al-Malik informed us, from Ata, who said: Usamah said: I entered with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, the House. He sat and praised Allah, extolled Him, magnified and declared His oneness. Then he stood to what was before him of the House and placed his chest, cheek and hands upon it. He said: Then he magnified, declared oneness and supplicated. Then he did that with all the corners. Then he left and faced the qiblah at the door and said: This is the qiblah, this is the qiblah, two or three times."
"22168","Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Salih ibn al-Akhdar narrated to me, al-Zuhri narrated to me, from Urwah, from Usamah, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, had directed him on a mission. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, passed away, and Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, asked him: What did he entrust to you. He said: He entrusted to me to raid Ubna in the morning, then burn."
"22169","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, al-Taymi narrated to us, from Abu Uthman, from Usamah ibn Zayd, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said: I stood at the gate of Paradise, and most of those who enter it are the poor, except that the people of wealth are detained, except the people of Fire, for they have been ordered to the Fire. And I stood at the gate of Fire, and most of those who entered it are women."
"22170","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Ash'ath, from al-Hasan, from Usamah ibn Zayd, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: The cupper and the cupped have broken fast."
"22171","Yahya, from Shu'bah, narrated to us, Habib ibn Abi Thabit narrated to me, from Ibrahim ibn Sa'd, who said: I heard Usamah ibn Zayd narrating to Sa'd. He said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: If the plague is in a land while you are not in it, do not enter it, and if it is in a land while you are in it, do not leave it."
"22172","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from al-Taymi, from Abu Uthman, from Usamah ibn Zayd, who said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to take me and al-Hasan and say: O Allah, I love them, so love them. Yahya said: al-Taymi said: I used to narrate it, and something entered me, so I said: I have narrated it for so and so, and I found it written with me."
"22173","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, al-Taymi narrated to us, and Isma'il, from al-Taymi, from Abu Uthman, from Usamah ibn Zayd, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said: I have not left among people after me a trial more harmful to men than women."
"22174","Yahya, from Abd al-Malik, narrated to us, Ata narrated to us, from Usamah ibn Zayd, that he entered, he and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, the House. He ordered Bilal, who closed the door. The House at that time was upon six pillars. He went until he came to the two pillars next to the door, the door of the Ka'bah, and sat and praised Allah, extolled Him, asked Him and sought His forgiveness. Then he stood until he came to what faced him from the back of the Ka'bah, and placed his face and body upon the Ka'bah, and praised Allah, extolled Him, asked Him and sought His forgiveness. Then he left until he came to each corner of the corners of the House, facing it with magnification, declaration of oneness, glorification, praise of Allah the Mighty and Majestic, seeking forgiveness and supplication. Then he left and prayed two rak'ahs outside the House, facing the Ka'bah. Then he left and said: This is the qiblah, this is the qiblah."
"22175","Yahya, from Sufyan, narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Uqbah narrated to me, from Kurayb, from Usamah ibn Zayd, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he moved, or poured forth, from Arafah and came to the pass where the rulers and caliphs dismount, he said: He urinated, and I brought him water, and he performed a good ablution between the two ablutions. Then he rode his mount. I said: The prayer, O Prophet of Allah. He said: The prayer is ahead of you. He said: He came to Jam' and called the establishment and prayed Maghrib. Then the rest of the people did not unpack until he called the establishment and prayed Isha."
"22176","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar and al-Thawri narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Uqbah, from Kurayb, from Usamah, who said: We left with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, from Arafah. When he reached, Ma'mar said: the mountain pass, and al-Thawri said: the pass, and he mentioned its meaning."
"22177","Waki' narrated to us, Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from his father, who said: I was sitting with Usamah, and he was asked about the pace of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he moved from Arafah. He said: He went al-anaq; when he found an opening he galloped, meaning above al-anaq."
"22178","Waki' narrated to us, from Ibn Dharr, from Mujahid, from Usamah ibn Zayd, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, poured forth with calmness upon him, and commanded them with calmness."
